### Real-Time Pipeline Execution - SSE & Console Output (Session: 2026-05-15)

Implemented real-time pipeline execution monitoring across both runpipelines and pipeline-run-history pages using SSE (Server-Sent Events) and polling fallback.

#### Architecture Overview

**Backend SSE Support:**
- Endpoint: `/api/pipeline-runs/{runId}/stream` - Returns SseEmitter
- Uses `CopyOnWriteArrayList<SseEmitter>` mapped by runId to support multiple concurrent connections
- Both pages can connect to the same runId and receive the same events simultaneously
- Events sent: `step-output`, `step-error`, `pipeline-complete`, `connected`

**Frontend SSE Implementation (both pages):**
- EventSource connection to backend SSE endpoint
- Event listeners for step-output, pipeline-complete, step-error
- Automatic reconnection on error (3 second delay)
- Fallback to polling (3 second interval) if SSE fails

